[2026-05-15T19:32:43] $ git commit -m "Enable JEPA multitask gating before consistency trials\n\nIJEPA and VJEPA now use the Phase2-A derived-dataset baselines and\nencoder-specific input layouts in the multitask diagnostic trainer. The B\nlambda sweep records single-GPU tmux launches, W&B runs, and A-vs-B gates\nbefore selecting checkpoints for consistency training.\n\nConstraint: Training remains server-local on sparsh-force-slip with manual push/pull only\nConstraint: JEPA checkpoints expose target_encoder weights rather than encoder/teacher prefixes\nRejected: Reuse 2026.05.11 JEPA baselines | they were trained on the original-data path, not the Phase1 derived dataset\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Keep VJEPA input as video/4-frame/3-channel when evaluating or training multitask decoders\nTested: py_compile; CLI help for IJEPA/VJEPA/+trainer.devices; one-batch IJEPA and VJEPA partially_shared smoke; four B trainings completed; B report/gate generated\nNot-tested: Git push; held for manual push/pull per user rule\n"
